    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "The Laurels is a spacious and light-filled detached dormer bungalow sitting peacefully on circa 0.33 Hectares / 0.81 Acre of glorious and sun-drenched landscaped gardens. \r\n\r\nThe property is presented in excellent condition throughout and will appeal to buyers looking for a fine family home in a sought-after location and close to all important amenities. \r\n\r\nThe accommodation extends to 248 Sq. M. / 2,669 Sq. Ft. (approx.) spanning over two levels. The layout at ground floor level comprises: entrance hall, sitting room, living room, kitchen/dining room, sunroom and utility room with a large hot press. Two good-sized double bedrooms (one with en-suite and both with walk-in wardrobes) complete the layout at ground floor level.\r\n\r\nThe layout at first floor level comprises: landing area, three well-proportioned bedrooms (one with walk-in wardrobe), WC and a study / home office with a shower room. \r\n\r\nGARDENS:\r\nThe Laurels sits on circa 0.33 Hectares / 0.81 Acre mature and private grounds. The property is fully walled at the road and is accessed through decorative wrought-iron vehicular gates. A tarmacadamed driveway is flanked on both sides by neat lawns with mature trees, herbaceous and flowering plants and conifer and Laurel hedging. There is extensive parking several cars to the front sides and rear of the property.\r\n\r\nA well-finished detached garage has a vehicular roller door to the front and a PVC glass panel pedestrian door to the side and window on opposite side. The garage has power and plug sockets and houses a Firebird oil burner. The sun-drenched decked area to the rear of the house is perfect for al-fresco dining and entertaining. The garden to the rear contains a well-appointed Greenhouse. \r\n\r\nLOCATION:\r\nThe Laurels is well-located in the townland of Barrettstown in the parish of Knocktopher. The property is just a 7-minute walk to the village of Knocktopher which has many important amenities including Centra Carroll’s Supermarket and Service Station, Scoil Aireagail mixed-gender secondary school, Scoil Phádraig primary school and Ballyhale Creche and Montessori School. Tirlán CountryLife store in Ballyhale is also close-by. \r\n\r\nThe property is just a 5-minute drive to Junction 10 on the M9 Motorway with easy access to Waterford, Kilkenny, Carlow, Kildare and Dublin. The travelling time to Dublin by car is 1-hour and 40-minutes approx.\r\n\r\nViewing of this fine family home is highly recommended."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "GROUND FLOOR\r\n\r\nEntrance Hall (including stairs) (2.98m x 2.65m + ((2.98m + 3.84m) / 2) x 0.87m + (8.11m x 1.21m): A black coloured Composite front door with glass insert open into a striking and spacious L-shaped entrance hall with double height vaulted ceiling. Bespoke made U-shaped staircase up to first floor level. Wood effect vinyl floor covering. Window to the front of the property. \r\n\r\nSitting Room (3.71m x 2.56m) + ((3.71m + 2.87m)/2) x 0.85m): A fine-sized room with a large picture window overlooking the front garden and driveway. Impressive white Marble open fireplace with a cast-iron insert, black Marble hearth and fitted with a multi-fuel stove. Ceiling coving and centre rose. Wood effect vinyl floor covering. \r\n\r\nLiving Room (4.37m x 5.08m): A cosy room positioned to the front of the property. Black and white tiled flooring. \r\n\r\nKitchen / Dining Room:6.76m x 4.19m): Exceptionally large and sun-drenched open plan room located to the rear of the property. Cream country-style wall and floor units with tiled backsplash, Granite effect laminate countertops and 1.5 ceramic bowl sink. Rangemaster all electric range cooker. Integrated extractor fan. Plumbing is in place for a dishwasher. Alcove for fridge/freezer. Fitted breakfast bar with space for two stools. This dining area can accommodate a large table and chairs for family dining and entertaining. Cast-iron multi-fuel stove with tiled backsplash. Two west-facing windows overlook the rear garden. PVC French doors open through to a sunroom. Tiled floor throughout.\r\n\r\nSunroom (3.91m x 3.65m): A triple aspect sun-drenched room with views of the gardens and the surrounding picturesque countryside. Vaulted ceiling with tongue and groove ceiling boards. PVC French doors lead out to the side of the property. Tiled floor throughout. \r\n\r\nUtility Room (2.12m x 3.44m): Fitted floor units with single drainer sink, tiled backsplash and Granite effect laminate countertops. Plumbing for washing machine and space for a tumble dryer or undercounter freezer.\r\n \r\nHot Press (2.12m x 0.74m): Large floor to ceiling and wall to wall built-in hot press with fitted shelving and hot water cylinder fitted in 2026. A PVC external door with frosted glass panel gives access to the rear of the property. Frosted window to the side of the external door. Tiled floor.\r\n\r\nBedroom One (4.19m x 3.73m): A spacious double bedroom located to the front of the property. Fitted carpet. \r\n\r\nEn-Suite (1.94m x 1.19m + 0.85m x 1.11m): Comprising a wet-room shower with a thermostatic shower. WC and wash hand basin with wall mounted mirror and overhead shaving light. Fully tiled walls and floor. Frosted gable end window.\r\n\r\nWalk-in Wardrobe (0.78m x 1.21m): Fitted with hanging space and shelving. Tiled floor and light. \r\n\r\nBedroom Two (3.91m x 3.08m + 0.92m x 1.11m): A large and bright double bedroom positioned to the rear of the property. Fitted carpet. \r\n\r\nWalk-in Wardrobe (1.87m x 0.98m): Built-in shelving and fitted carpet. \r\n\r\nBathroom (2.40m x 4.18m): Exceptionally large and bright with a frosted window to the rear. Enclosed shower cubicle fitted with a Triton T90si pumped electric shower, WC and wash hand basin with fitted glass shelf and wall mounted mirror. Built-in bath with matching tiled surround. \r\n\r\nFIRST FLOOR\r\nLanding (including stairs) (0.99m x 1.87m + 3.76m x 1.00m) + 2.20m x 0.78m): A spacious and bright area with a west-facing Velux window fitted in the roof to the rear of the property. Fitted carpet along with a fitted runner carpet on the staircase. \r\nBedroom Three (4.41m 4.36m + 1.58m x 0.78m): A sun-drenched and very large dual aspect double bedroom a south-east facing dormer window to the front and a south facing gable end window. Stained tongue and groove floorboards. \r\nWalk-in Wardrobe (1.96m x 1.51m): Fitted shelving and handing space. Tiled floor. \r\n\r\nWC (2.33m x 1.51m): Comprising WC and wash hand basin. Fully tiled walls and floor. West-facing Velux window fitted in the roof to the rear. \r\n\r\nBedroom Four (4.66m x 2.29m) + 1.55m x 0.75m): A double bedroom with a south-east facing to the front of the property. Stained tongue and groove floorboards. Access to eaves storage. \r\n\r\nBedroom Five (3.28m x 4.06m) + (1.57m x 0.75m): A dual aspect double bedroom with s dormer window to the front and a gable end window. Stained tongue and groove floorboards. \r\n\r\nHome Office / Study (4.66m x 2.49m): A spacious and bright room to the rear with a West-facing Velux window fitted in the room. Access to eaves storage. Stained tongue and groove floorboards. \r\n\r\nWC / Shower Room (3.26m x 1.49m) + 1.73m x 0.32m): Comprising an enclosed shower cubicle fitted with a thermostatic shower. WC and wash hand basin with wall mounted mirror and glass shelf. Fully tiled walls and vinyl floor covering. Two extractor fans."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "SPECIAL FEATURES:\r\nSubstantial five bedroomed detached dormer bungalow\r\nLarge sun-drenched site with mature gardens (circa 0.33 Hectares / 0.81 Acre)\r\nMinute's walk to Knocktopher village\r\nDetached garage\r\n5-minute drive to Junction 10 on the M9 Motorway\r\n20-minute drive to Kilkenny City Centre\r\n\r\nSERVICES:\r\nOil fired central heating \r\nZoned heating system with two independently controlled zones\r\nTimer on Immersion\r\nAlarm with one security camera at the front of the property\r\nBroadband with Vodafone \r\nTV cable - Sky dish in place\r\nConnected to mains water (Water Purification System) \r\nUpgraded Septic Tank to a modern sewage treatment system"
